; coalesce.test — kernscope-coalesce: per-memory-op coalescing ANALYSIS
; (todo 42, Wave 7).
;
; Analysis-only pass: classifies every addrspace(1) (NVPTX global) load/store
; into the todo-15 vocabulary (contiguous-128B | contiguous-partial |
; strided | unknown-pattern) under the 32B-sector model, via SCEV on the
; pointer relative to the tid intrinsic. NO transforms (PreservedAnalyses::all
; — llvm-diff must be byte-identical).
;
; Fixtures (tests/pass/Inputs/coalesce/):
;   * fully_coalesced.ll — tid-indexed float load+store, stride 1 element ->
;     contiguous-128B (efficiency 1.0), 4 sectors. GOLDEN.
;   * strided.ll         — stride 8 elements -> 8x sector overfetch ->
;     strided (commit 2).
;   * unknown.ll         — indirect (loaded) index -> unknown-pattern, never
;     claimed coalesced (commit 2).
;
; The classification-count report hook (todo-42 report): opt
; -kernscope-coalesce-report prints
; "kernscope-coalesce: <fn>: N global accesses (F fully, P partial,
; U uncoalesced, K unknown); widest access W B; vectorized V" to stderr
; (asserted below).
;
; REQUIRES: no-gpu

; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes='kernscope-coalesce,verify' -S %S/Inputs/coalesce/fully_coalesced.ll -o %t.out
; RUN: %llvm_tools_dir/llvm-diff %S/Inputs/coalesce/fully_coalesced.ll %t.out

; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes=kernscope-coalesce -kernscope-coalesce-report -S %S/Inputs/coalesce/fully_coalesced.ll -o %t.rep 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REPORT

; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes=kernscope-coalesce -kernscope-coalesce-report -S %S/Inputs/coalesce/strided.ll -o %t.str 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REPORT-STRIDED
; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes=kernscope-coalesce -kernscope-coalesce-report -S %S/Inputs/coalesce/unknown.ll -o %t.unk 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REPORT-UNKNOWN

; ============================================================================
; The todo-42 acceptance DELTA assertion, on the COMMITTED showcase IR
; (tests/pass/fixtures/<kernel>/before.ll — real clang-21 output; the committed
; showcase artifacts are inputs here, so the suite pins the before/after
; story end to end):
;
;   * layernorm: the canonical pipeline (kernscope-as1 + the real pass
;     chain) raises vector_width 1 -> 4 — after.ll contains <4 x float>
;     loads (48 loads / 12 chains) and before.ll has none. ASSERTED.
;   * the classifier on the real kernels (canonical form): gemm's stride-1
;     b-load fully + tid.y-dependent unknowns; softmax's runtime-stride
;     accesses unknown; layernorm's thread-per-row accesses uncoalesced.
;
; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes='kernscope-as1,kernscope-tile,kernscope-promote,kernscope-vectorize,kernscope-pad,verify' -kernscope-vectorize-report -S %S/fixtures/layernorm/before.ll -o %t.ln 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DELTA-LN
; RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DELTA-VEC --input-file %t.ln
; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes='kernscope-as1,kernscope-coalesce' -kernscope-coalesce-report -S %S/fixtures/gemm/before.ll -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GEMM
; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes='kernscope-as1,kernscope-coalesce' -kernscope-coalesce-report -S %S/fixtures/softmax/before.ll -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SOFTMAX
; RUN: opt -load-pass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -passes='kernscope-as1,kernscope-coalesce' -kernscope-coalesce-report -S %S/fixtures/layernorm/before.ll -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LN

; The analysis must be a no-op on the IR (byte-identical llvm-diff above).
; Fully coalesced (stride-1 float): 32 lanes x 4 B = 128 B = 4 sectors ->
; efficiency 1.0 (the brief §3.1 golden, same counts as the todo-15 PTX
; analyzer asserts).
; REPORT: kernscope-coalesce: coalesce_kernel: 2 global accesses (2 fully, 0 partial, 0 uncoalesced, 0 unknown); widest access 4 B; vectorized 0

; Stride-8 float: 32 sectors per warp for 128 B of useful data (the todo-15
; 32-sector golden) -> strided.
; REPORT-STRIDED: kernscope-coalesce: strided_kernel: 2 global accesses (0 fully, 0 partial, 2 uncoalesced, 0 unknown); widest access 4 B; vectorized 0

; Indirect (loaded) index: the gather load stays affine (fully), the two
; data-dependent accesses are unknown-pattern — never claimed coalesced.
; REPORT-UNKNOWN: kernscope-coalesce: unknown_kernel: 3 global accesses (1 fully, 0 partial, 0 uncoalesced, 2 unknown); widest access 8 B; vectorized 0

; ---- the todo-42 delta, asserted on the real showcase IR ------------------
; The layernorm showcase through the canonical pipeline: 48 scalar loads
; vectorized into 12 <4 x float> chains (vector_width 1 -> 4; the
; before.ll has no vector loads — see the report's vector_width_before=1).
; DELTA-LN: kernscope-vectorize: {{.*}}: vectorized 48 loads, 0 stores (12 chains)
; DELTA-VEC: load <4 x float>
; DELTA-VEC-NOT: load <8 x float>

; ---- the classifier on the real kernels (canonical form) ------------------
; gemm: the stride-1 b-load is fully coalesced; the tid.y-dependent
; a-load/c-store are honestly unknown-pattern (warp-varying rows).
; GEMM: kernscope-coalesce: {{.*}}: 3 global accesses (1 fully, 0 partial, 0 uncoalesced, 2 unknown); widest access 4 B; vectorized 0

; softmax: runtime row length -> per-lane stride not a compile-time
; constant -> all accesses unknown-pattern, never claimed coalesced.
; SOFTMAX: kernscope-coalesce: {{.*}}: 4 global accesses (0 fully, 0 partial, 0 uncoalesced, 4 unknown); widest access 4 B; vectorized 0

; layernorm: thread-per-row -> per-lane stride 256 B -> 32 sectors per
; warp for 128 B of useful data -> all uncoalesced (honest; the report
; records the vectorize-after state: 12 partial + 16 uncoalesced).
; LN: kernscope-coalesce: {{.*}}: 64 global accesses (0 fully, 0 partial, 64 uncoalesced, 0 unknown); widest access 4 B; vectorized 0
